WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
An ancient Hindu hymn,
the Hymn of Creation,

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.850
asks how everything began.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.200
It ends with a startling thought: perhaps
even the one who watches from the highest

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.410
heaven does not know.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.500
For most Hindus, time is a circle.

6
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.030
Universes come into
being, last, and dissolve,

7
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.930
again and again.

8
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.550
If the universe is born,
dies and is born again,

9
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.300
which part of the cycle are we in now?

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.510
In this mission, you'll
measure a day of Brahma:

11
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.140
1,000 cycles of ages.

12
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:39.290
Then you'll weigh up whether this ancient
picture of time fits modern science.

13
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:44.270
Your mission: find out which part of the
cosmic cycle many Hindus say we are in

14
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:44.830
now.
